  "description": "Loft extension of the rear double pitched roof area. Side walls are proposed to be raised, new window to the rear elevation be added, 4 skylights are proposed to be integrated to the new roof as well as 1 skylight to the existing roof above the staircase.\n\nThis proposal would not need to alter or create new access, layout any new street, construct any associated hard-standings, means of enclosure or means of draining the land/buildings.\n\nThe building accomodates 2 flats, one of which uses Ground Floor only (5A) with a seperate entrance from side elevation and the other (5) is spread accross First and Second Floors as well as getting access from Ground Floor and is subject to our application hereby. To gain an extra room of 18.77 sqm that enhances the flat's potential as a family home.\n\nThe rear double pitched roofs of all neighbouring properties seem to have been raised already.\n\nThe height of the part of the roof raised, would NOT exceed the height of the highest part of the roof of the existing building\n\nThe materials used in any exterior work WILL be of a similar appearance to those used in the construction of the exterior of the existing building",
  "development_type": "Minor all other minor developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: [insert plan numbers/documents].\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building, unless otherwise shown on the approved plans.\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the appearance of the area."
  ],
